From 97b53ec9a1e179ff5413f1ffa2b1d00b735e40a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:46:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add real SMS sending (Twilio/Textbelt) with actual delivery
 in Personalize
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Personalize previously stopped at a SEND decision — it drafted a message and
chose SMS as the channel, but nothing was ever actually sent (documented
explicitly in run_personalize's docstring: "Does NOT send... those aren't
built yet"). This was true for every channel, not just SMS.

Adds backend/integrations/sms.py, a real connector that sends via:
  1. Twilio, if real (non-placeholder) TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID/AUTH_TOKEN/
     FROM_NUMBER are configured
  2. Textbelt otherwise — real delivery via textbelt.com's free, no-signup
     demo key, so a fresh checkout can send a genuine text without any
     account setup
  3. A logged-only mock as the last-resort fallback, so a bad provider
     response can never crash a demo run

Wires it into orchestrator/service.py's new dispatch_send(), called from the
personalize endpoint and the converse follow-up path: on a real send it
records an outbound ConversationTurn and transitions the prospect
QUALIFIED -> CONTACTED. Other channels (email/linkedin/voice) are left as
decision-only for now — no connector exists for them yet, and this stays
explicit in code rather than silently claiming they're wired up too.

Verified backend/integrations/sms.py end-to-end against Textbelt's real API
(test key, so it exercises the full HTTP/auth/response-parsing path without
spending the shared quota) — the request/response cycle works.

